## Troubleshooting / Problems Encountered

### Problem 1: ESP32 failed to upload

Solution: Used BOOT and RESET sequence and lowered upload speed to 115200.

### Problem 2: Wrong boot mode detected

Solution: Forced ESP32 into flash/download mode using BOOT button.

### Problem 3: Access Point did not appear

Solution: Added `WiFi.softAP(ap_ssid, ap_password);` correctly inside setup().

### Problem 4: Telegram bot not responding

Solution: Corrected Chat ID and bot token configuration.

## Final Report

In this project, I configured the ESP32-CAM to operate in both Station Mode and Access Point Mode. The ESP32 connected to WiFi while also creating its own wireless network called “CSN150_Lab_Test”. I integrated Telegram functionality to remotely send photos from the ESP32-CAM to my phone. This project helped me better understand IoT security, wireless networking, troubleshooting, and remote monitoring systems.

This project was tested in a controlled lab environment using my own devices and network for educational purposes only.

